From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-bandix-plus: traffic monitor only

The app is reduced to the traffic monitor: the interface overview with
the current rate and volume per interface, the realtime chart, the
device list with the rate and the volume for a period, the usage
ranking and the traffic timeline. Removed:

- on the status page: interface rate limits (the gear button on the
  interface cards and the limit lines), the guest control section
  (default guest limits and the whitelist), the scheduled rate limits
  and the hostname dialog behind the device Settings button, deleting
  devices, and the update badge;
- on the settings page: the update check, the feedback link and the
  API bind address (the service keeps 127.0.0.1, see the bandix-plus
  patch).

The status page no longer polls the four rate-limit lists every second
and no longer asks GitHub for updates when it is opened. The service
status (apk list, ubus, curl to the API) is read every 10 seconds
instead of every second; the overview and the realtime chart still
refresh every second.

rpcd answers only the methods of the monitor (health, snapshot,
overview, devices, trend, histogram, usage ranking, version, status,
restart); the others return "Method is disabled in this build". The ACL
grants reading the monitor data and writing only the settings and the
service restart. Before, the read part of the ACL also held
checkUpdate.

Traffic persistence is described and preselected on the settings page:
without it the usage ranking and the traffic timeline are lost on every
restart of the service.

